! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.55 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.62) --
! THE CHANNEL SYMBOL TABLE SEARCH.
!
! Forty-four lines and ALL FORTY-FOUR COMPILE -- no comment rows and
! no heading box, solid code from 003105.40 to 003147.00.
!
! >>> THIS PAGE CLOSES THE GAP. <<<  printed p.54's last line (56) is
! "L IOD3  TI,1,5.0(L IODX),0.0(L XSU)" at 003104.40, a full word,
! ending at 003105.40 -- line 1 here.  And line 44 is "B,L ETA" at
! 003147.00, one half word, ending at 003147.40 -- printed p.56 line
! 5.  With pp.56, 57 and 58 that makes printed pp.54-58 CONTIGUOUS TO
! THE BIT, which is what strap/prosa.py requires before the image may
! hold any of them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! An IOD card's channel name is looked up in the symbolic channel
! table, entered if absent, and the unit slot is pointed at it.
!
!   lines 1-5    carry the tape reel count and tape type into the
!                unit table and the IOREQ slot.
!   lines 6-12   L OOPSC, the search proper -- and line 12 is a HALT.
!   lines 13-24  L IOD4 / L CHAN: enter the channel, compute where in
!                the table it landed, and join the channel name to
!                the unit name.
!   lines 25-33  L ENTER: a new RLSYM, its count bumped, then back.
!   lines 34-44  L SET / L SETA: the null-channel case and the
!                direct move to the associated channel slot.
!
! >>> LINE 12 IS A HALT, AND THE THIRD THIS PROJECT HAS TRANSCRIBED.
! <<<  "BD,$" at 003116.40 printing 003116.44 00 -- branch disabled
! to its own address -- commented "-INTERNAL CHANNEL TABLE EXCEEDED".
! The others are printed p.6 line 1's "BD,$  -LOOP" and printed p.54
! line 55's "BD,$  -INTERNAL UNIT TABLE".  All three are table
! overflows or error stops, which is what a machine with no operating
! system under it can do about one.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> L BLANK APPEARS TWICE, ONCE BARE AND ONCE NOT, AND THE TWO
! ROWS DIFFER EXACTLY AS THE dds RULE PREDICTS <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 18 is "K(BU,48),L BLANK" -- dds WRITTEN -- and compiles
! 060000.21 10.  printed p.56 line 11 is "K,L BLANK" -- dds NOT
! written -- and compiles 060600.21 10.  The difference is 0600, the
! BYTE SIZE, which printed p.54 carries as
! "L BLANK SYN(BU,48,6),(8)2736.0" and derived by measuring a blank
! count in pixels.
!
! SO THE SAME SYMBOL, ON TWO PAGES, PRINTS TWO DIFFERENT SECOND
! GROUPS, and the one that differs is the one that wrote nothing.
! That is C22-6531 printed p.31's sentence demonstrated on a single
! operand -- "data properties (dds) associated with Y ... are
! transferred to A" -- and it is the cleanest instance this project
! has: no second symbol, no second length, only the presence or
! absence of the written dds.
!
! Lines 1 and 3 are the same shape: "L,L TAPEC" and "M+1,L TAPEC",
! both bare, both compiling 007000 = length 7 out of printed p.54's
! "L TAPEC SYN(BU,7),(8)2601.31".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY SYMBOL OFF THIS PAGE IS ALREADY PLACED, AND IT POINTS BOTH
! WAYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   BACKWARD, to printed p.54:
!     line 24  B,L FOUND  003055.50 00 -> 003055.40
!     line 33  B,L FOUND  003055.50 00 -> 003055.40
!     line 44  B,L ETA    003103.50 00 -> 003103.40
!     line 34  L SET is this page's own label at 003137.40, which
!              printed p.54 line 53 ("BAEZ,L SET") SYNs.
!   FORWARD, to printed p.58:
!     line 37  BZRZ,L NORM  003237.74 C0 -> 003237.40
!     line 43  BAEZ,L NORM  003237.76 C6 -> 003237.40
!
! AND IT CONFIRMS printed p.56's L COUNT INDEPENDENTLY.  Line 31 is
! "ST(BU,7),L COUNT" compiling 002601.53 80, the same 002601.53 that
! p.56 line 51's "L(BU,7),L COUNT,46" gives.  Two pages, two rows,
! one bit address.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! L XSC IS $8, AND TWO ROWS SAY SO INDEPENDENTLY
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 6's "LX,L XSC,L SYMCX" has ".20" -> bits 19-22 = 1000 = 8 in
! its J field, and line 26's "L(BU,7),L XSC+.11,0.0" has the ADDRESS
! 000030 = word 0o30 = 16+8.  The same shape that pinned L XNT on
! printed p.58 line 23, here split across two rows instead of one.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FOUR EXPRESSIONS, AND TWO OF THEM ARE NEGATIVE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  4  "L TAPE+.60"   -> 002733.74   (0o74 = 60)
!   line 29  "L WORKX+.14"  -> 000032.16   (0o16 = 14)
!   line 30  "L RLCT-.8(L WORKX)" -> 002606.70; L RLCT is 002607.0,
!            and eight bits back is 002606 bit 56 = 0o70.
!   line 32  "L SYMC-1."    -> 002657; L SYMC is 002660.
! None of the four needs a new symbol -- each is an offset from one
! this page or another already fixes.
!
! THREE LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location: lines 1
! ("003105.40 *"), 16 ("003121.00 *") and 30 ("003134.40 *").
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> 900 dpi WAS NOT ENOUGH FOR ONE BYTE, AND THE PAIR WAS B/8
! AGAIN <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 40's opcode byte was transcribed as 80 from a 900 dpi render
! and is B0.  listing_typography.md 11 already names this pair -- "B
! and 8 are the only pair in 0-9A-F that differ mainly in one
! vertical stroke, and that stroke is the first thing a worn drum
! printer loses" -- and the project's memory records printed p.3 line
! 10 as the instance that cost three commits.  THE MEMORY ALSO SAYS
! TO READ HEX AT 900 dpi, AND HERE 900 dpi GOT IT WRONG.
!
! AT 1800 dpi IT IS NOT CLOSE: the glyph has a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT
! STROKE with two bowls hung off it, which is a B; an 8 is two closed
! round bowls with no straight edge anywhere.  Rendering one byte at
! 1800 dpi costs one pdftoppm.
!
! AND THE CORPUS SETTLED IT WITHOUT THE ASSEMBLER.  The assembler
! disagreeing with a transcription is a PROMPT to look again, not an
! answer -- the listing is the oracle, not the model.  Five rows
! already transcribed from earlier pages print "V+" as B0:
!
!   000702.00  000025.06 B0   X13 2A  V+,$3,$5
!   001167.40  002152.34 B0   V+,$14,S X CHAN
!   001540.40  000036.34 B0   V+,$14,$14
!   001622.00  000035.32 B0   V+,$13,$13
!   001623.00  002152.32 B0   V+,$13,S X CHAN
!
! so B0 is V+'s byte on five independent pages.  (M+1 also shows B0
! -- lines 3 and 30 here -- but in the SECOND half word of a
! full-word VFL instruction, which is a different field; line 40 is a
! half-word index operation and its single byte is its own.)
!
! THE PRACTICE THIS ADDS: when the assembler and a hex byte disagree,
! re-render THAT BYTE at 1800 dpi and grep the corpus for the
! mnemonic.  Two cheap checks, neither of which is "believe the
! model".

        SLC, (8)3105.40

! ---- index registers ----------------------------------------------
LIODX   SYN, $3
LXIO    SYN, $5
LXSU    SYN, $7
LXSC    SYN, $8
LWORKX  SYN, $10
! ---- stand-ins confirmed by pages already transcribed -------------
LTAPEC  SYN(BU,7), (8)2601.31
LBLANK  SYN(BU,48,6), (8)2736.0
TTYPE   SYN, 0.3
LFOUND  SYN, (8)3055.40
LETA    SYN, (8)3103.40
LNORM   SYN, (8)3237.40
LRLCT   SYN, (8)2607.0
LCOUNT  SYN, (8)2601.53
! ---- new on this page ---------------------------------------------
LTAPE   SYN, (8)2733.0
LSYMCX  SYN, (8)2566.0
LSYMC   SYN, (8)2660.0
TRLSYM  SYN, 0.11

        SLC, (8)3105.40

! ---- the tape reel count and tape type ----------------------------
        L, LTAPEC                    ! line 1  -ENTER THE TAPE REEL
                                      !           COUNT
        ST(BU,7), .50(LXSU)          ! line 2  -IN THE TAPE UNIT TABLE
        M+1, LTAPEC                  ! line 3  -AND BUMP BY ONE
        L(BU,4), LTAPE+.60, 0.0      ! line 4  -STORE TAPE TYPE IN
        ST(BU,4), TTYPE(LXIO)        ! line 5  -  IOREQ SLOT

! ---- the symbolic channel table search ----------------------------
        LX, LXSC, LSYMCX             ! line 6  -IS CHANNEL IN SYMBOLIC
LOOPSC  L(BU,48), 0.0(LXSC), 0.0     ! line 7  -   CHANNEL TABLE.
        BRZZ, LIOD4                  ! line 8  -   NO----STEP DOWN.
        K(BU,48), 4.0(LIODX), 0.0    ! line 9
        BAEZ, LCHAN                  ! line 10 -   YES----STEP DOWN.
        CB+, LXSC, LOOPSC            ! line 11 -TRY AGAIN ON NON-ZERO
                                      !           COUNT.
        BD, $                        ! line 12 -INTERNAL CHANNEL TABLE
                                      !           EXCEEDED
LIOD4   TI, 1, 4.0(LIODX), 0.0(LXSC) ! line 13 -ENTER CHANNEL IN
                                      !           TABLE.
LCHAN   V-I, LXSC, LSYMC             ! line 14 -COMPUTE WHERE IN TABLE
        SV, LXSC, $R                 ! line 15
        ST(BU,7), 0.57(LXSU), 46     ! line 16 -CHAN NAME WITH THE
                                      !           UNIT NAME
        L(BU,48), 4.0(LIODX)         ! line 17 -IS CHANNEL SYMBOL
                                      !           BLANK
        K(BU,48), LBLANK             ! line 18
        BZAEZ, LENTER                ! line 19 -   NO----STEP DOWN.
        CM0000(BU,7), TRLSYM(LXIO)   ! line 20
        CM1111(BU,1), 0.48(LXSU)     ! line 21 -SET THE UNIT SLOT TO
                                      !           NULL CHAN
        V+I, LXSC, LSYMC             ! line 22 -RESTORE THE CHAN IX
        CM0000(BU,64), 0.0(LXSC)     ! line 23 -CLEAR A BLANK FROM
                                      !           THE CHAN TBL
        B, LFOUND                    ! line 24 -BRANCH

! ---- a new RLSYM --------------------------------------------------
LENTER  V+I, LXSC, 1.0               ! line 25 -INCREASE BY ONE FOR
                                      !           RLSYM
        L(BU,7), LXSC+.11, 0.0       ! line 26
        ST(BU,7), TRLSYM(LXIO)       ! line 27
        Z, LWORKX                    ! line 28 -STORE RLSYM SHIFTED
                                      !           3 BITS
        ST(BU,7), LWORKX+.14, 0.0    ! line 29 -   FOR SUBSEQUENT
                                      !           SORT.
        M+1(BU,8), LRLCT-.8(LWORKX)  ! line 30 -ADD ONE TO PROPER
                                      !           COUNT.
        ST(BU,7), LCOUNT             ! line 31
        V+I, LXSC, LSYMC-1.          ! line 32 -RESTORE CHANNEL INDEX.
        B, LFOUND                    ! line 33 -BRANCH

! ---- the null-channel case ----------------------------------------
LSET    LF(BU,48), 4.0(LIODX)        ! line 34 -IS THE CARD CHANNEL
                                      !           NULL
        KF(BU,48), LBLANK            ! line 35
        BZAE, LSETA                  ! line 36 -IF NOT NULL CONTINUE
                                      !           LOOKING
        BZRZ, LNORM                  ! line 37 -YES A NULL CHANNEL
LSETA   LX, LXSC, LSYMCX             ! line 38 -IS CHANNEL IN THE
                                      !           SYMBOLIC
        L(BU,7), 0.57(LXSU), 46      ! line 39 -MOVE INDEX DIRECTLY
                                      !           TO THE
        V+, LXSC, $R                 ! line 40 -ASSOCIATED CHAN SLOT
        L(BU,48), 0.0(LXSC), 0.0     ! line 41 -   CHANNEL TABLE.
        K(BU,48), 4.0(LIODX), 0.0    ! line 42
        BAEZ, LNORM                  ! line 43 -   YES----NORMAL
                                      !           RETURN.
        B, LETA                      ! line 44
        END, LOOPSC

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKED ROWS -- all forty-four.
